462
00:39:47.430 --> 00:40:07.370
Audio shared by Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): That's where hybrid storage of your private key comes in. Instead of choosing between edge storage or cloud storage for your private keys, you combine them. For example, your wallet might store the key securely on your device, but also back it up in the cloud, encrypted so only you can unlock it. But what if you forget your password or lose access entirely?

463
00:40:07.370 --> 00:40:18.250
Audio shared by Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): That's where social recovery adds another layer. Imagine splitting your recovery key into pieces and giving one share each to a few trusted friends or to devices you own.

464
00:40:18.250 --> 00:40:33.919
Audio shared by Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): No single person can unlock your identity, but if you collect enough shares, say, 3 out of 5, you can reconstruct the key and recover your DID. This way, you're not relying only on a cloud provider, and you're not left stranded if your phone dies.

465
00:40:33.920 --> 00:40:42.710
Audio shared by Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): Hybrid storage with social recovery blends convenience, resilience, and trust, making decentralized identity practical for real-world use.

